  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "A pilotless fighter plane flew in circles over Dayton for hours. In October 1925, residents looked up in total disbelief at a rogue aircraft roaring through the clouds with an empty cockpit.",
        "visual_query": "vintage 1920s biplane airplane flight",
        "visual_fallback": "old airplane flying"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The experimental bomber had broken free from its moorings at McCook Field in Ohio, surging into the sky with no one at the controls.",
        "visual_query": "historic 1920s aviation airfield hangar",
        "visual_fallback": "vintage airfield"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Airplanes of the 1920s lacked any automated flight stabilization systems. So how did this heavy machine keep itself upright and airborne without a pilot to steady it?",
        "visual_query": "vintage airplane cockpit instruments",
        "visual_fallback": "old cockpit"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Investigators later found the answer in the twisted wreckage. A stuck throttle cable locked the rudder and ailerons into a balanced, perpetual turn.",
        "visual_query": "vintage airplane engine mechanical parts",
        "visual_fallback": "old machinery"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The runaway aircraft simply flew in a massive mechanical circle until it exhausted its fuel supply and glided down into an empty farm field.",
        "visual_query": "rural 1920s farmland aerial view",
        "visual_fallback": "open field landscape"
      }
    ],
